# Feature Implementation: Complete Novel & Short Story Content Management System

## 1. Project Objective

Upgrade the existing Urdu Novels website by implementing a complete content management and display system for novels, PDF downloads, and short stories.

The objective is to ensure that uploading a novel's PDF is not the only content provided to users. Every novel should have a rich, informative detail page containing its summary, author information, author notes, important notices, sneak peeks, book details, download information, and related content.

All content must be manageable manually through Sanity Studio. The frontend must fetch and display the content dynamically from Sanity instead of relying on hardcoded content.

**Important:** This is an enhancement to the existing project, not a complete rebuild. Inspect the existing codebase, Sanity schemas, queries, routes, components, styling, and color palette before making changes. Preserve existing functionality and follow the established architecture.

## 2. Pages to Update

Implement the required functionality across these existing website sections:

1. All Novels page
2. Individual Novel Detail page
3. Download PDF page
4. Short Stories listing page
5. Individual Short Story Detail page
6. Shared content cards and related-content sections

Maintain the existing navigation, branding, footer, responsive behavior, and established color palette.

## 3. Sanity CMS Schema Updates

Extend the existing Sanity schemas instead of creating duplicate schemas or breaking existing documents.

### A. Novel Schema

Each novel must support the following fields.

**Basic Information**
- Novel Title (Urdu)
- English Title / Transliteration (optional)
- URL Slug
- Novel Cover Image
- Short Tagline
- Author (reference to the Author document)
- Genres / Categories
- Language
- Novel Status: Completed, Ongoing, or Discontinued
- Publication Date
- Last Updated Date

**Novel Description**
- Short Description for cards and listings
- Full Novel Summary
- About This Novel
- Story Introduction
- Content Warning (optional)
- Author's Note
- Important Note for Readers

Use appropriate Sanity field types, validation, and optional fields where necessary. Long-form Urdu content must support paragraphs and appropriate text formatting through Portable Text where suitable.

**Novel Specifications**
- Number of Pages
- Number of Chapters
- File Format
- File Size (where available)
- Reading Availability: Online, PDF Download, or Both
- Featured Novel toggle
- Trending Novel toggle

Do not require fields that are not relevant to every novel.

### B. Novel Sneak Peeks

Add a manually manageable `sneakPeeks` array to the Novel schema.

Each sneak-peek entry must support:
- Preview Image
- Optional Caption
- Optional Chapter or Page Reference
- Optional Display Order

Allow multiple preview images for one novel. The admin must be able to add, remove, and reorder the images in Sanity Studio.

Display these images in a responsive gallery on the novel detail page. Clicking an image should open a larger preview using an accessible lightbox.

### C. Novel PDF and Download Information

Add a dedicated download section to the Novel schema.

Fields:
- Downloadable PDF File
- Download Display Title
- Download Description or Instructions
- File Format
- File Size, when available
- Optional External Download URL
- Optional Download Button Label

Use Sanity's file asset field for uploaded PDF files.

The frontend must display the download button only when a valid PDF asset or permitted download URL exists. Do not show broken download buttons or fabricated file information.

If a PDF is uploaded, generate the appropriate downloadable URL from the Sanity file asset. Do not hardcode file URLs.

The download action must work on desktop and mobile. Preserve secure and appropriate access to the file.

### D. Online Reading and Chapters

Support an optional online-reading section.

Fields:
- Enable Online Reading
- Online Reading Introduction
- Chapters Array

Each chapter must support:
- Chapter Number
- Chapter Title
- Chapter Content
- Optional Chapter Image
- Display Order

Chapter content should use Portable Text where appropriate.

If online reading is unavailable, hide the chapter-reading interface and retain the PDF download functionality.

Do not create empty chapter sections when a novel has no chapters.

### E. Author Schema

Create or extend a reusable Author document.

Fields:
- Author Name
- URL Slug
- Profile Image
- Short Biography
- Detailed Biography (optional)
- Social or Official Website Links (optional)

Connect novels to authors through Sanity references.

Display the author's information on novel detail pages and provide a link to the author's other novels where an author page or filtered listing is supported.

Avoid duplicating the author's biography inside every novel document.

### F. Short Story Schema

Create or extend a separate Short Story document, reusing appropriate shared structures where practical.

Fields:
- Story Title (Urdu)
- English Title / Transliteration (optional)
- URL Slug
- Cover Image (optional)
- Author
- Genre / Category
- Short Description
- Full Story Summary or Introduction
- Story Content
- Author's Note
- Important Note (optional)
- Language
- Publication Date
- Estimated Reading Time (optional)
- Featured toggle
- Trending toggle
- Related Stories (optional)
- Related Novels (optional)
- SEO Title
- SEO Description

Support multiple paragraphs and Urdu right-to-left text formatting.

A short story may be published as readable website content without requiring a PDF.

If a downloadable file is provided, support an optional story PDF attachment using the same download principles as novels.

## 4. All Novels Page

Upgrade the existing All Novels listing page.

Every novel card should display available information:
- Cover image
- Urdu novel title
- Author name
- Genre
- Short description, where appropriate
- Rating, only if a genuine rating system exists
- PDF availability indicator
